WEBVTT

00:00:00.620 --> 00:00:02.950
Previously on Yu-Gi-Oh! VRAINS:

00:00:02.950 --> 00:00:08.950
Light Ignis, in order to advance 
your Ignis unification plan...

00:00:08.950 --> 00:00:12.660
...you rewrote the Wind Ignis’s 
program to force it to be your ally.

00:00:12.660 --> 00:00:14.940
You must be joking, Lightning!

00:00:14.940 --> 00:00:16.900
You’ll go that far?

00:00:16.900 --> 00:00:19.840
For the future of the Ignis!

00:00:19.840 --> 00:00:22.770
For the future?  Stop joking!

00:00:22.770 --> 00:00:26.770
Everything you do is full of lies!

00:00:26.770 --> 00:00:28.880
You shouldn't regret it.

00:00:28.880 --> 00:00:34.210
It may have started as a lie, but my ideas 
are heading towards the correct future.

00:00:34.210 --> 00:00:40.190
Then I'll mercilessly and 
completely correct you!

00:00:40.190 --> 00:00:43.600
This is the end, Light Ignis!

00:00:43.600 --> 00:00:46.160
Return to nothing!

00:00:46.520 --> 00:00:51.700
Borreload Dragon attacks Estrangement Dragon-

00:00:54.100 --> 00:00:59.240
I just linked my program with Jin 
Kusanagi’s consciousness data.

00:00:59.640 --> 00:01:05.440
If I lose, Jin Kusanagi’s consciousness 
data will be completely destroyed.

00:01:24.280 --> 00:01:30.290
Our lives aren't forever

00:01:31.090 --> 00:01:37.080
We wander, searching for the meaning of life

00:01:38.030 --> 00:01:44.400
Even if it's not the right direction, 
just keep looking forward

00:01:44.850 --> 00:01:50.970
Sharing hope for the future

00:01:50.970 --> 00:01:57.720
tell me  We're searching for 
memories lost in the darkness

00:01:57.910 --> 00:02:04.950
I feel your flame  Your 
impulses pierce the light

00:02:05.090 --> 00:02:11.660
I want to share your pain

00:02:52.350 --> 00:02:53.860
Revolver...

00:02:53.860 --> 00:02:56.090
That’s dirty, Lightning!

00:02:56.090 --> 00:03:02.090
I’m showing you how to use a hostage.

00:03:02.090 --> 00:03:07.270
It was the right decision 
not to end him earlier.

00:03:07.270 --> 00:03:09.720
By the way, Revolver...

00:03:09.720 --> 00:03:14.510
I'm also linked to Spectre’s 
consciousness data.

00:03:14.510 --> 00:03:18.120
So if you defeat me, he’ll vanish too.

00:03:18.120 --> 00:03:22.700
Don’t you think this is the 
appropriate way to use weaklings?

00:03:23.520 --> 00:03:30.720
What’s wrong?  Previously, you were fine 
having many innocent victims in order to kill us.

00:03:30.720 --> 00:03:33.690
Kill the few so many can live.

00:03:33.690 --> 00:03:36.300
That’s your strategy.

00:03:36.300 --> 00:03:38.700
So you don't need to hesitate.

00:03:38.700 --> 00:03:42.170
Now do it, Revolver!

00:03:43.680 --> 00:03:46.270
Don’t underestimate me, Light Ignis!

00:03:46.270 --> 00:03:47.400
Borreload Dragon-

00:03:47.400 --> 00:03:48.980
Don’t do it, Revolver!

00:03:49.910 --> 00:03:54.560
If you attack, you’ll revert 
to how you used to be!

00:03:54.560 --> 00:03:57.070
We’ve come this far together.

00:03:57.070 --> 00:04:02.100
Because you're different than before!

00:04:02.800 --> 00:04:07.390
We came here prepared to make sacrifices.

00:04:07.390 --> 00:04:09.220
I know.

00:04:09.220 --> 00:04:13.930
Isn’t that why you 
defeated Shoichi Kusanagi?

00:04:14.840 --> 00:04:18.060
Kusanagi was willing to make that sacrifice.

00:04:18.060 --> 00:04:19.940
But not him!

00:04:19.940 --> 00:04:23.380
He was dragged into the Lost 
Incident!  And this one too!

00:04:23.380 --> 00:04:26.000
He hasn’t done anything wrong!

00:04:27.150 --> 00:04:31.120
Do you want to create another 
Lost Incident victim?

00:04:32.540 --> 00:04:34.640
You’ve changed.

00:04:34.640 --> 00:04:38.060
You chose not to battle Soulburner earlier!

00:04:38.060 --> 00:04:40.030
Earlier...

00:04:47.640 --> 00:04:50.420
Humans are funny.

00:04:50.420 --> 00:04:55.870
My enemy Playmaker is saving my life.

00:04:55.870 --> 00:04:58.320
I’m not saving you!

00:04:58.320 --> 00:05:03.850
But if I abandon them, that 
means we’ve truly lost!

00:05:04.900 --> 00:05:11.090
That’s true.  Nothing will 
be sadder if he vanishes now.

00:05:11.090 --> 00:05:12.190
What?

00:05:12.190 --> 00:05:18.200
Back then, I already knew 
how to invade the network.

00:05:18.200 --> 00:05:23.600
It was pathetic how scared he 
was, but I kept accessing him.

00:05:24.200 --> 00:05:28.710
And I learned how to terrify people.

00:05:30.060 --> 00:05:33.180
He truly entertained me.

00:05:33.840 --> 00:05:39.650
Electrocuted after losing a duel, 
just as he regains consciousness...

00:05:39.650 --> 00:05:44.600
...I show him an illusion that help 
has arrived and he can escape.

00:05:44.600 --> 00:05:51.420
The moment he feels safe, I 
drop him into a pit of terror.

00:05:53.030 --> 00:05:56.030
He starts crying and raging.

00:05:59.140 --> 00:06:05.180
But I tormented him a bit too much, 
so his soul completely broke.

00:06:05.180 --> 00:06:13.780
You’re an evil error program that 
shouldn’t exist in this world!

00:06:13.780 --> 00:06:18.420
I'll completely bury you!

00:06:19.160 --> 00:06:22.540
If you really mean it, you should attack.

00:06:22.540 --> 00:06:26.600
That is, if you can destroy 
these foolish humans.

00:06:27.700 --> 00:06:33.360
You spoke of free will.  How 
our species was spineless.

00:06:33.360 --> 00:06:36.040
Then show me what you're willing to do!

00:06:36.860 --> 00:06:42.120
I set one card and end my turn.

00:06:42.120 --> 00:06:48.820
When the turn ends, Estrangement Dragon's 
effect sends it to the graveyard.

00:06:53.300 --> 00:07:01.400
By making friends and walking the path of 
justice, you're no longer willing to go that far.

00:07:01.400 --> 00:07:05.370
Now what should I do to you…

00:07:07.120 --> 00:07:09.470
What a cheater!

00:07:09.470 --> 00:07:12.000
That Light Ignis…

00:07:12.000 --> 00:07:16.620
The old Revolver wouldn't 
hesitate to make a decision.

00:07:16.620 --> 00:07:20.570
But now, Revolver is unsure.

00:07:20.570 --> 00:07:23.200
And the Ignis figured that out.

00:07:23.200 --> 00:07:27.820
We created a terror.

00:07:27.820 --> 00:07:31.930
Revolver, this will end you.

00:07:33.630 --> 00:07:34.560
My-

00:07:34.560 --> 00:07:35.720
Wait.

00:07:36.920 --> 00:07:42.580
I told you I wouldn't let you 
do any more dirty tricks.

00:07:42.580 --> 00:07:44.080
Bohman…

00:07:44.080 --> 00:07:47.110
I can’t stand what you’re doing.

00:07:47.710 --> 00:07:51.580
Soulburner was a fair duelist.

00:07:51.580 --> 00:07:58.190
But Windy spoiled-  No, 
you spoiled that duel.

00:07:58.760 --> 00:08:01.190
I'm disappointed in you.

00:08:01.190 --> 00:08:04.530
I won’t let that kind of duel happen again!

00:08:06.080 --> 00:08:07.530
But Bohman-

00:08:07.530 --> 00:08:11.700
I'll hold on to Jin Kusanagi and 
Spectre’s consciousness data.

00:08:13.780 --> 00:08:15.240
What?

00:08:20.380 --> 00:08:22.980
Are they having a falling out?

00:08:24.620 --> 00:08:25.980
Bohman…

00:08:26.960 --> 00:08:28.380
You can't.

00:08:28.380 --> 00:08:32.420
Your program can no longer meddle with me.

00:08:37.600 --> 00:08:39.860
There are no hostages anymore.

00:08:39.860 --> 00:08:44.970
Lightning, defeat Revolver 
with your own skills.

00:08:47.460 --> 00:08:51.520
Continue the duel without distress.

00:08:53.180 --> 00:08:54.750
I won't thank you.

00:08:54.750 --> 00:08:56.980
I know.

00:08:58.700 --> 00:09:02.420
Then I’ll crush you with power!

00:09:02.420 --> 00:09:07.800
Light Ignis, I'll never forgive you.

00:09:14.230 --> 00:09:17.540
My turn!  I draw!

00:09:18.220 --> 00:09:22.040
I summon Armatos Legio Sica.

00:09:23.740 --> 00:09:27.480
Appear!  The circuit that guides the light!

00:09:27.480 --> 00:09:32.080
The summoning condition is one 
Level 4 or lower Armatos Legio.

00:09:32.080 --> 00:09:33.820
Link Summon!

00:09:33.820 --> 00:09:38.920
Appear!  Link 1 Armatos Legio Decurion!

00:09:38.920 --> 00:09:43.060
I activate the spell card, Armatos Fulgur!

00:09:43.060 --> 00:09:47.270
I tribute an Armatos Legio 
Link Monster on the field.

00:09:47.270 --> 00:09:50.670
I Special Summon a different monster from the

00:09:50.670 --> 00:09:54.940
Extra Deck with equal Link 
Markers as the tributed monster.

00:09:55.770 --> 00:10:02.580
I tribute Decurion to Special 
Summon Armatos Legio Eques Flamma!

00:10:05.680 --> 00:10:11.520
The Link Spell, Armatos Legio 
Plumbum Trident’s effect!

00:10:11.520 --> 00:10:14.920
I return a Link Monster in 
my graveyard to my deck.

00:10:14.920 --> 00:10:20.130
And I Special Summon an Armatos Legio 
from my graveyard next to its link.

00:10:20.130 --> 00:10:27.910
I return Decurion to my Extra Deck and 
Special Summon Armatos Legio Magnus Dux!

00:10:32.220 --> 00:10:34.410
It resurrected again.

00:10:34.410 --> 00:10:38.950
When Borreload Dragon’s 
effect lowers ATK...

00:10:38.950 --> 00:10:44.160
...Judgment Arrows’s effect will 
raise Magnus Dux’s ATK to 5000.

00:10:44.160 --> 00:10:50.630
Your Borreloads have 3000 
ATK, and you have 2000 LP.

00:10:50.630 --> 00:10:53.360
You’ll exactly run out of LP.

00:10:54.280 --> 00:10:59.060
Oh, before you're gone, let 
me tell you one good thing.

00:10:59.900 --> 00:11:03.360
Unlike you, I'll get to the point.

00:11:03.360 --> 00:11:04.710
Tell me what?

00:11:04.710 --> 00:11:08.820
About your father, Dr. Kogami.

00:11:08.820 --> 00:11:14.190
Revolver, you misunderstand one major topic.

00:11:14.190 --> 00:11:15.560
What?

00:11:15.560 --> 00:11:23.760
You think SOL Technologies infected Kogami 
with a computer virus, but that’s not true.

00:11:24.420 --> 00:11:30.470
After the Lost Incident, we built 
Cyberse World inside the network.

00:11:30.470 --> 00:11:37.940
Cyberse World created Data Material, 
which helped SOL Technologies greatly.

00:11:37.940 --> 00:11:42.680
Back then, I ran the 
simulation you mentioned.

00:11:43.440 --> 00:11:50.480
Strangely at the same time, Kogami also ran 
another simulation on the Ignis's future.

00:11:50.480 --> 00:11:57.180
The result showed the Ignis 
would be humanity's enemy.

00:11:57.180 --> 00:12:06.300
If Kogami ran additional simulations, he 
would eventually learn that I was the cause.

00:12:06.300 --> 00:12:12.310
So I took the initiative and 
eliminated that problem.

00:12:12.310 --> 00:12:19.280
Yes, I was the one who implanted 
the computer virus in Kogami.

00:12:19.680 --> 00:12:21.250
What?

00:12:21.820 --> 00:12:23.630
Unable to decide whether

00:12:23.630 --> 00:12:30.100
to take responsibility for the Lost 
incident, SOL Technologies confined Kogami.

00:12:30.730 --> 00:12:38.120
Since we were both inside the same 
company, I got through the server.

00:12:38.120 --> 00:12:44.650
Fortunately, Kogami complained to SOL’s 
higher-ups about the danger of the Ignis.

00:12:44.650 --> 00:12:47.840
So they were already at odds.

00:12:47.840 --> 00:12:52.050
I didn’t expect you'd resurrect Kogami.

00:12:52.050 --> 00:13:00.590
But when you did, Kogami completely believed 
SOL Technologies implanted the virus.

00:13:00.590 --> 00:13:05.820
So Lightning was the one 
who created the virus!

00:13:05.820 --> 00:13:08.800
That's why it's such a powerful program!

00:13:08.800 --> 00:13:17.240
Thanks to that., I was able to get plenty of 
time to build my new secret weapon - Bohman.

00:13:17.240 --> 00:13:21.780
I see.  You’re the one who hurt my father!

00:13:22.440 --> 00:13:26.180
We made a huge misunderstanding.

00:13:26.180 --> 00:13:31.160
Our revenge should've been 
against the Light Ignis!

00:13:31.160 --> 00:13:37.180
It was fun to see you fight with 
all your might, not realizing

00:13:37.180 --> 00:13:40.630
your revenge should've been directed at me.

00:13:40.630 --> 00:13:44.780
I’ll send you to meet Kogami.

00:13:44.780 --> 00:13:50.760
Battle!  Magnus Dux attacks 
Borreload eXcharge Dragon!

00:13:50.760 --> 00:13:54.440
Borreload Dragon’s effect activates!

00:13:54.440 --> 00:13:56.660
Anti Enemy Varrett!

00:13:56.660 --> 00:14:01.520
One monster’s ATK and DEF decrease by 500!

00:14:01.520 --> 00:14:06.100
And you can’t activate effects 
against this effect's activation!

00:14:09.390 --> 00:14:14.160
But due to Judgment Arrows’s 
effect, its ATK are doubled.

00:14:14.160 --> 00:14:17.520
If he takes this attack, Revolver loses!

00:14:17.520 --> 00:14:21.240
I activate the Continuous Trap, Borrel Ring!

00:14:21.240 --> 00:14:24.040
By tributing one Borrel Link Monster,

00:14:24.040 --> 00:14:28.370
I put a counter on this card for 
every one of its Link Markers!

00:14:28.370 --> 00:14:31.720
I tribute Borreload Dragon!

00:14:32.580 --> 00:14:36.120
Borreload Dragon has 4 Link Markers!

00:14:36.120 --> 00:14:40.560
So I put four counters on Borrel Ring.

00:14:40.560 --> 00:14:47.920
When your monster attacks my 
monster, I remove one counter.

00:14:47.920 --> 00:14:51.440
My monster can't be 
destroyed in that battle,

00:14:51.440 --> 00:14:56.280
and your monster loses 
100 ATK for each counter!

00:14:58.010 --> 00:15:02.480
Now Magnus Dux has 2200 ATK.

00:15:02.480 --> 00:15:05.800
So you lowered its ATK even more.

00:15:06.980 --> 00:15:10.720
But now, Judgment Arrows’s effect!

00:15:11.700 --> 00:15:15.690
Even if I can’t destroy 
it, you still take damage.

00:15:21.300 --> 00:15:24.270
I end my turn.

00:15:24.740 --> 00:15:28.510
You weren’t able to defeat me!

00:15:29.400 --> 00:15:32.300
But you only have 600 LP left.

00:15:32.300 --> 00:15:36.820
No matter what you try, if 
my attack succeeds next turn-

00:15:36.820 --> 00:15:39.000
Why don’t you just accept it?

00:15:39.000 --> 00:15:44.440
You know you'll lose before 
your next turn comes.

00:15:45.660 --> 00:15:49.260
Revolver is going to turn this around?

00:15:49.260 --> 00:15:54.870
Borreload eXcharge Dragon still 
has one Overlay Unit left.

00:15:55.600 --> 00:16:00.340
I see!  If the same attack 
as last turn gets through…

00:16:01.400 --> 00:16:04.310
My turn!  I draw!

00:16:04.680 --> 00:16:07.950
Borreload eXcharge Dragon’s 
effect activates!

00:16:07.950 --> 00:16:14.440
By using one Overlay Unit, 
one monster loses 600 ATK.

00:16:14.440 --> 00:16:17.150
Anti Enemy eXcharge!

00:16:19.290 --> 00:16:25.300
Then I can select a Borrel monster in 
the graveyard and Special Summon it!

00:16:25.300 --> 00:16:28.460
Resurrect, Borreload Dragon!

00:16:30.800 --> 00:16:37.840
Battle!  Borreload eXcharge 
Dragon attacks Magnus Dux!

00:16:42.780 --> 00:16:43.750
Fire!

00:16:45.720 --> 00:16:49.690
Borreload Dragon’s effect activates!

00:16:49.690 --> 00:16:52.720
Anti Enemy Varrett!

00:16:54.860 --> 00:16:55.980
All right!

00:16:55.980 --> 00:17:03.100
Now even if he uses Judgment Arrows, 
Borreload eXcharge has more ATK than Magnus Dux!

00:17:03.100 --> 00:17:07.640
If this attack succeeds, 
Lightning will take 200 damage.

00:17:07.640 --> 00:17:15.400
And if Borreload Dragon’s attack destroys 
Eques Flamma, Lightning will run out of LP.

00:17:15.400 --> 00:17:22.080
Before I use Judgment Arrows, I 
activate Magnus Dux’s effect!

00:17:22.080 --> 00:17:28.600
For every monster co-linked to this card, I 
return a card on the field or graveyard to the hand!

00:17:28.600 --> 00:17:32.000
I return Armatos Gloria to my hand!

00:17:32.000 --> 00:17:35.600
The Continuous Trap, Armatos Gloria's effect!

00:17:35.600 --> 00:17:40.470
When it's the target of an effect 
while in the Spell & Trap Zone...

00:17:40.470 --> 00:17:43.840
...all monsters on my field are destroyed.

00:17:45.580 --> 00:17:49.620
Now, Eques Flamma’s effect!

00:17:49.620 --> 00:17:53.580
When an effect destroys it 
while it’s co-linked...

00:17:53.580 --> 00:18:01.830
...we both take damage equal to the original 
ATK of the monster co-linked to it!

00:18:01.830 --> 00:18:03.560
What?

00:18:03.960 --> 00:18:06.260
I won’t lose.

00:18:06.260 --> 00:18:15.720
Me - an Ignis that transcends humanity 
- can’t lose to someone like you!

00:18:26.140 --> 00:18:27.550
Revolver!

00:18:28.160 --> 00:18:31.800
No way…  Revolver was…

00:18:33.560 --> 00:18:38.230
The Light Ignis destroyed 
itself to get a tie.

00:18:39.860 --> 00:18:41.200
Revolver!

00:18:41.200 --> 00:18:43.740
Pull yourself together, Revolver!

00:18:44.620 --> 00:18:50.620
I didn’t expect the Light 
Ignis to destroy itself.

00:18:50.620 --> 00:18:52.320
I let my guard down.

00:18:52.320 --> 00:18:56.210
Revolver!  You did well!

00:18:56.210 --> 00:19:02.050
When I was young, I'd lay down in a field of 
flowers and look up at the sky,

00:19:02.050 --> 00:19:04.560
like how I’m doing now.

00:19:05.060 --> 00:19:08.700
I'm reminded of those times.

00:19:08.700 --> 00:19:12.070
I had no troubles back then.

00:19:12.070 --> 00:19:17.520
I was just excited about the 
world that spread before my eyes.

00:19:20.360 --> 00:19:24.120
I’m leaving before you.

00:19:25.080 --> 00:19:31.720
I leave the rest to you, Playmaker... and Ai.

00:19:37.580 --> 00:19:41.390
He called me by my name.

00:19:43.800 --> 00:19:45.880
Revolver…

00:19:52.400 --> 00:19:54.000
What about Lightning?

00:19:59.460 --> 00:20:03.110
I’m still alive.

00:20:04.080 --> 00:20:05.400
What?

00:20:05.400 --> 00:20:07.550
Why only Lightning?

00:20:10.550 --> 00:20:12.520
Lightning.

00:20:12.520 --> 00:20:18.530
You didn’t give me all of Jin 
Kusanagi’s consciousness data.

00:20:18.530 --> 00:20:22.000
And you converted it into extra LP.

00:20:22.000 --> 00:20:28.010
Yes.  I'll do anything to win.

00:20:28.010 --> 00:20:31.500
That's my mission.

00:20:33.120 --> 00:20:37.780
Bohman, I'll give you everything.

00:20:39.040 --> 00:20:42.380
Show me mercy.

00:20:44.160 --> 00:20:51.130
You caused chaos by deceiving 
everyone with your wicked ideas.

00:20:52.360 --> 00:20:54.330
Bohman…

00:20:54.330 --> 00:21:00.940
But you did everything so you could live.

00:21:00.940 --> 00:21:08.260
Among the Ignis, you may 
have been most human.

00:21:09.350 --> 00:21:13.420
Fine.  I accept everything.

00:21:19.560 --> 00:21:26.360
Bohman, my soul is with you.

00:21:39.560 --> 00:21:42.180
Lightning gave himself to Bohman.

00:21:43.260 --> 00:21:47.920
Now Bohman has acquired five Attributes.

00:21:48.640 --> 00:21:50.890
The stage is set.

00:21:50.890 --> 00:21:57.360
I've completed my training.  
Accept my duel, Playmaker!

00:21:57.360 --> 00:22:03.370
Yes.  It’s the final fight, Bohman!

00:22:05.620 --> 00:22:09.560
I was told repeatedly

00:22:09.560 --> 00:22:17.040
Only tales of dreams

00:22:17.390 --> 00:22:24.010
Is my life precious?

00:22:24.270 --> 00:22:26.980
Make up for  Make up for

00:22:27.370 --> 00:22:34.520
The next sentimental

00:22:39.350 --> 00:22:45.770
I'm not a machine

00:22:48.490 --> 00:22:52.210
I cry a single tear

00:22:53.700 --> 00:22:57.410
A single answer moves me

00:22:58.600 --> 00:23:07.790
We helplessly sing for someone we can't reach

00:23:08.410 --> 00:23:13.190
Are you ready?

00:23:13.720 --> 00:23:18.570
Oh oh oh

00:23:19.090 --> 00:23:23.770
Are you ready?

00:23:24.390 --> 00:23:30.880
Are you ready?

00:23:37.880 --> 00:23:44.800
As arrows of light rain down on 
people, screams fill LINK VRAINS.

00:23:44.800 --> 00:23:52.040
These sacrifices are necessary for 
the Ignis to create a new world?

00:23:52.040 --> 00:23:56.080
There's only one person who can stop him!

00:23:56.080 --> 00:23:59.380
Playmaker, we can only count on you!

00:23:59.380 --> 00:24:03.980
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! VRAINS:
Door to the New World

00:24:03.980 --> 00:24:05.980
Into the VRAINS!
